## 1. Move Semantics: The Default

### Exercise 1.1 — Take it by value

**Goal**: feel a by-value parameter consume the caller's value.

**Info**: A `String` parameter is a move: the caller's binding is gone after the call. The function owns the value and may do anything with it — including just measuring it.

**Objectives**

- return the byte length of `text`, taking ownership of it
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §1.1 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: the body is one method call on `text`.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
/// Take ownership of `text` and return its byte length.
///
/// TODO: replace `todo!()` with the length.
fn consume_len(text: String) -> usize {
    todo!()
}

// --- check (do not modify) ---
assert_eq!(consume_len(String::from("hello")), 5);
assert_eq!(consume_len(String::new()), 0);
assert_eq!(consume_len(String::from("é")), 2);
println!("Exercise 1.1 passed");
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Exercise 1.2 — A conditional move

**Goal**: move a value on one branch only, and see what the caller is left with.

**Info**: `Some(text)` moves the payload into the variant. On the `None` branch nothing is moved — but the caller cannot know which branch ran, so from the caller's side the value is *maybe moved* either way.

**Objectives**

- return `Some(text)` when its byte length is strictly greater than `threshold`
- return `None` otherwise, leaving the payload unowned by the result
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §1.2 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: one `if` on `text.len()`; the move happens inside the `Some(...)`.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
/// Return `Some(text)` when it is longer than `threshold`, `None` otherwise.
///
/// TODO: replace `todo!()` with the conditional move.
fn drain_if_long(text: String, threshold: usize) -> Option<String> {
    todo!()
}

// --- check (do not modify) ---
assert_eq!(drain_if_long(String::from("hello"), 3), Some(String::from("hello")));
assert_eq!(drain_if_long(String::from("hi"), 3), None);
assert_eq!(drain_if_long(String::new(), 0), None);
assert_eq!(drain_if_long(String::from("abc"), 2).as_deref(), Some("abc"));
println!("Exercise 1.2 passed");
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Exercise 1.3 — Moves compose

**Goal**: move two values into containers, then hand the container on.

**Info**: `push`, tuple construction and `Some(...)` all take their payload by value — each is a move of a non-`Copy` value, and none of them copies anything.

**Objectives**

- append `extra` to `items` (a move into the `Vec`)
- return the `Vec`
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §1.3 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: declare the parameter `mut` so you may push into it.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
