    todo!()
}

// --- check (do not modify) ---
let mut n = 5;
assert_eq!(add_twice(&mut n, 2, 3), 10);
assert_eq!(add_twice(&mut n, -10, 10), 10);
let mut zero = 0;
assert_eq!(add_twice(&mut zero, 0, 0), 0);
println!("Exercise 4.3 passed");
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Exercise 4.4 — Never return a borrow of a local

**Goal**: hit the rule behind `E0106` from the design side: what the function *should* return.

**Info**: A `&str` return type ties the result to some input the caller owns. When the function has no suitable input — it built the text itself — the only honest return is an owned `String`.

**Objectives**

- return `text` with a `*` prefix and a `*` suffix, as an owned value
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §4.4 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: `format!` returns exactly what the contract needs.
</VSCode.Cell>
