## 5. Slices as Borrowed Views

### Exercise 5.1 — Slice the middle out

**Goal**: take a sub-range of a slice as a borrowed view.

**Info**: `&data[start..end]` computes a new fat pointer over the same elements — no copy. The bounds follow the same rules as string slicing, minus the UTF-8 concern: any index range is valid.

**Objectives**

- return the elements of `data` from index `start` (inclusive) to `end` (exclusive)
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §5.1 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: one range expression on the slice, returned as `&[i32]`.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
